# Golden: the modern note vocabulary (D39/D42) over a |C|F| change, country varD.
# chord1 is a guitar STRUM (ChordGesture::kStrumUp/Down fans the live chord with a
# fixed micro-stagger); the kLead part is a telecaster lick where kScaleDegree
# notes stay diatonic to the KEY across the F chord while a kInterval blue-3 grace
# tracks the CHORD root (so it moves C->F, the scale degrees do not).
key C major
port open out virt as synth
chord out synth:4
style load country
style route drums synth:10
style route bass synth:2
style route chord1 synth:3
style route lead synth:7
style section varD
seq new verse
seq add C 1bar
seq add F 1bar
seq loop on
seq play
transport start
advance 7680
quit
